        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## `uv` and `mamba`\n",
        "\n",
        "### `uv`\n",
        "[`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) is a new Python package and project manager, written in Rust. Besides all its other functionalities, it can be treated as a drop-in replacement of `pip`. All commands we mentioned above can be rewritten by replacing `pip` with `uv pip`. `uv` fix many issues of Python built-in package and project managers. In addition it runs much faster.\n",
        "\n",
        "### `mambda`\n",
        "[`mamba`](https://github.com/mamba-org/mamba) is a reimplementation of the `conda` package manager in `C++`. It can be treated as a drop-in replacement of `conda`. All commands we mentioned above can be rewritten by replacing `conda` with `mamba`. One of the reasons to use `mamba` over `conda` is that `mamba` runs so much faster than `conda`.\n"
